mation in addition to the GAAP metrics and provide comparability and consistency to prior periods. Constant currency revenues translate revenues denominated in foreign currencies to the United States dollar, net of the effect of foreign currency hedges, at rates consistent with those in the prior year. The Company calculates Argentina inflation as the revenue growth not attributable to either transaction growth or the change in price (revenue divided by principal).","context":"Non-GAAP Measures","section":"Business Development","block":38,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-326110","form":"8-K","filedAt":"2026-07-30","reportDate":"2026-07-30","cik":"0001365135","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1365135/000119312526326110/wu-ex99_1.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/1ebd5ff387b3b791a7411279ff1ddc438c9342c95f905c8b4cbc6ce379023fa6.bin","sha256":"1ebd5ff387b3b791a7411279ff1ddc438c9342c95f905c8b4cbc6ce379023fa6"}},{"id":"27a93c319560196de73857de46b79dc8a9a1cb7df72441eacc44ad1e26b15e2f","quote":"Reconciliations of non-GAAP to comparable GAAP measures are available in the accompanying schedules and in the “Investor Relations” section of the Company’s website at https://ir.westernunion.com.","context":"Western Union presents non-GAAP financial measures because management believes that these metrics provide meaningful supplemental information in addition to the GAAP metrics and provide comparability and consistency to prior periods. Constant currency revenues translate revenues denominated in foreign currencies to the United States dollar, net of the effect of foreign currency hedges, at rates consistent with those in the prior year. The Company calculates Argentina inflation as the revenue growth not attributable to either transaction growth or the change in price (revenue divided by principal).","section":"Business Development","block":39,"table":null,"attributio